          "distinct": false,
          "id": "97c89e78484c7469d60e8f2378ca34f9e60f9503",
          "message": "docs(research): bounded context sharing between fleet agents — three-channel design (#4187)\n\n* docs(research): design record — bounded context sharing between fleet agents\n\nThree strictly-separated channels (lineage handoff / method memory / live\nstate) so cross-agent context does not grow without bound:\n\n- Channel A: per-task ledger, one slot per stage, REPLACE-not-append, so\n  size is O(stages) rather than O(attempts). Rides the marker comments the\n  fleet already writes; no new storage.\n- Channel B: curated method memory, pull-not-push, indexed one-liners with\n  lazy load and a hard per-agent retrieval budget. PKG-backed.\n- Channel C: a rule, not a store — never memorise what one API call derives.\n\nAdmission is restricted to non-derivable, decision-changing method knowledge,\nwhich is what makes the corpus asymptote rather than grow linearly; corpus\nsize vs cumulative tasks is the stated health metric and falsification test.\n\nGrounded in this project's own measurements: pkg-query halved Opus tokens\n(adopted) while outline-first and terse were both measured and rejected, so\nevery channel is measurement-gated against worker yield with stop conditions\ndeclared in advance.\n\nRefs #1111\n\n* docs(research): give the task-ledger fence a language (MD040)\n\nmarkdownlint-cli2 0.18.1 red on this file at research/agent-context-sharing.md:74\n\"MD040/fenced-code-language Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\".\nIt is the only error in the 420-file lint. The block is a pseudo-schema sketch of\nthe per-stage ledger slots, not runnable code, so `text` is the honest tag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-27T12:06:39Z",
